<div class="section-wrapper" id="faq" >
    <div class="section-label" style="background-color: #6b46c1;"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div class="section-content">
        <div class="bench-faq-wrap"><div class="bench-faq-text"><div class="bench-faq-list"><div class="bench-faq-item"><h3 class="bench-faq-q">Which processor is faster, Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU) or Apple M5?</h3><div class="bench-faq-a"><p>It depends on the workload: in single-core performance the Apple M5 leads by 7%, in multi-core workloads the Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU) leads by 51%.</p></div></div><div class="bench-faq-item"><h3 class="bench-faq-q">What are the technical differences between Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU) and Apple M5?</h3><div class="bench-faq-a"><p>The most important differences at a glance:</p><table class="vs-faq-diff"><thead><tr><td></td><th scope="col">Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU)</th><th scope="col">Apple M5</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Cores / Threads</th><td>14 / 14</td><td>9 / 9</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Turbo Frequency</th><td>4.51 GHz</td><td>4.61 GHz</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TDP</th><td>50 W</td><td>17 W</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Integrated graphics (iGPU)</th><td>Apple M4 Pro (20 Core)</td><td>Apple M5 (10 Core)</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Release date</th><td>Q4/2024</td><td>Q4/2025</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="bench-faq-item"><h3 class="bench-faq-q">Which processor is more efficient, Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU) or Apple M5?</h3><div class="bench-faq-a"><p>The Apple M5 is rated at 17 W TDP, the Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU) at 50 W. TDP is the thermal budget for cooling, not actual power use. In a notebook, battery life also depends heavily on the display and workload.</p></div></div><div class="bench-faq-item"><h3 class="bench-faq-q">Which processor is better for gaming?</h3><div class="bench-faq-a"><p>Games rely mainly on single-core performance, and there the Apple M5 is 7% ahead of the Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU). Actual frame rates also depend on the GPU in the laptop – the iGPU or a dedicated graphics chip.</p></div></div><div class="bench-faq-item"><h3 class="bench-faq-q">Is it worth upgrading from the Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU) to the Apple M5?</h3><div class="bench-faq-a"><p>Purely for performance the upgrade is hardly worth it: the Apple M5 is only marginally ahead of the Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU). Because the CPU is usually soldered, a new laptop would be needed anyway; display, battery and ports then often matter more.</p></div></div></div></div></div>
    </div>
</div>




<div class="section-wrapper" id="reviews">
    <div class="section-label" style="background-color: #f56021;"><h2>User Reviews</h2></div>
    <div class="section-content">
      
        <script src="/ajax/cpu_rating_v2.js?v=1790893855" async></script>
        <div class="rating-summary-box">

            <div class="rating-info">
              <h3>Your rating</h3>
              <p>Here you can rate one or both of the processors. The average rating of <b>Apple M4 Pro (14-CPU 20-GPU)</b> is <b>4.8 stars</b> (472 ratings), while <b>Apple M5</b> has received <b>4.6 stars</b> (445 ratings).<br />
<br />
Click on the stars to rate one or both processors.</p>

